From 8d6f728e1a9d8a410d81d663346fb12ff28a38a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heappi <heappi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:58:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] snapshot: folds relative to an anchor layer

JS_SetSnapshotAnchor() keeps a copy of the current base as the anchor;
JS_SNAPSHOT_FOLD writes a chained checkpoint relative to the anchor
instead of the current base and promotes the written state, so a fold
holds only what changed since the shared layer. Tombstones are tracked
in both bases. JS_ReadSnapshotChainAnchored() rebuilds the anchor from
the state after a given checkpoint while applying a chain, so a restored
runtime can fold again. tests/snapshot/test_fold.c covers the round
trips, a second fold from a restored runtime, and a stale fold.
